<title>PAKISTAN: Ship with 13,125 tonnes of sugar reaches Karachi.</title>
<headline>Ship with 13,125 tonnes of sugar reaches Karachi.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The vessel M.V. Harmony Breeze has reached Karachi Port with 13,125 tonnes of Indian sugar and will start unloading on Wednesday, a port official said.</p>
<p>Pakistan bought 50,000 tonnes of Indian sugar in December at $350 and $360 per tonne for delivery by January 11.</p>
<p>Some 25,000 tonnes of sugar was to be transported by sea and the remaining 25,000 by rail via the Wagah border near Lahore.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
